From: theycallmeboxy <82409831+theycallmeboxy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 21:03:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: gate the per-draw blend and depth-bounds sysval
 compares on their dirty state

cmd_prepare_draw_sysvals() (2.51% of PanVK's samples in the Arkham
dxvk-cs profile) compared and stored, on every draw, the 8 blend
descriptors and the depth-bounds, depth-bounds-enable and sample-count
sysvals, then ran its 3-4 bitset AND/IS_EMPTY passes over the dirty
sysvals even when nothing was dirty.

- The blend descriptors are written only by blend_emit_descs(), which now
  flags them; the compare loop runs only after that.
- The depth-bounds block runs only when the depth-bounds enable or bounds,
  the rasterization sample count or RENDER_STATE (attachments; meta
  restore and the state resets set it too) is dirty.
- With no sysval changed, the shader-usage masking is skipped: it would
  find nothing.

blend_emit_descs() also flagged the FS push uniforms on every run, which
re-uploaded the FS FAU block after any blend-state change. The sysval
compare already flags them when a descriptor or a blend constant the FS
reads changes; the upload is still forced when needs_shader or
shader_loads_blend_const flips, because blend constants are not tracked
while unused.

first_vertex and base_instance are still stored on every draw.

PANVK_NO_SYSVAL_GATE=1 does every compare and the FS upload again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QAYrqSPd4TgpVaKLqz5cYR

Purpose: D3: CPU per draw: the blend-descriptor sysval compare runs only after blend_emit_descs ran, the depth-bounds/sample-count block only on its dirty bits or RENDER_STATE, the mask passes only when a sysval changed; FS push uniforms are re-uploaded on blend changes only when needs_shader/shader_loads_blend_const flips. PANVK_NO_SYSVAL_GATE=1 reverts (try it first if blending is wrong right after a blend-state change)
Upstream-commit: none
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (Anbernic RG477M, Dimensity 8300, v11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21 / MediaTek
Dependencies: none; applies on the full g615-v11-csf series after rg477m/024
Validation test: draw-path batch rg477m/023-027 on the device (drawcpu bench, DXVK pattern, 20,000 draws x 20 reps, pinned A715 at max clock, 10 interleaved runs per build): 543.6 -> 467.9 ns per recorded draw (-14%); with rg477m/024, 025 and 027 switched off 501.8 (the three together about -7%); PanProbe 38/38 x2; Arkham Asylum (CPU-bound DXVK, quietd Stock, 10 interleaved rounds + 3) gameplay fps unchanged (median 36.4 base vs 36.55), launch failures 0/13 base vs 2/13 (known B5 signatures, Fisher p~0.48, n.s.); combined build next.so (15c3385bbe40, rg477m/023-037): PanProbe 38/38 x2 (unsafe profile 37/38, only the bc_decode raw readback, by design); 16-game boot sweep 2026-10-25 in quietd Stock mode: Hades 60, Jupiter Hell 59, Risk of Rain 2 38, Moonlighter 60, Megabonk 60, Portal 2 60, Gladius 60, Crysis 3 Remastered 60 fps; Arkham Asylum to the menu; Factorio and Ashes menus render as before; Descenders, Tomb Raider, Doom 3 BFG and Metro 2033 match their known states; 0 GPU faults; Serious Sam bot benchmark A-B-B-A compat 49.2/52.7 vs next 53.3/51.1 fps; Arkham Asylum 20-round interleaved A/B 2026-10-25 (quietd Stock), base rg477m vs next: launch failures 1/20 vs 0/20 (session total 1/33 vs 4/36, not significant; B5 signatures also seen on the stock driver), gameplay fps median 36.4 vs 36.5, speckcount on 3 gameplay frames per run 0-1 px in both arms (base 2 runs with 1 px, next 3 runs with 1 px; the old specks bug gave tens to hundreds): no specks
